REMARKS:
Small-Boat Harbor has berthing capacity for approximately four-hundred-and-thirteen vessels.  Float 3, 402- by 10-foot with 32-, 42-, and 50-foot stalls; Float 4, 
390- by 10-foot with 32-, 42-, and 75-foot stalls; 
Float 5, 318- by 8-foot with 31-foot stalls; Floatý6,  304- by 6-foot with 23-foot stalls; Float 7, 192- by 6-foot with 24-foot stalls; and connecting float with 17-foot stalls.  Two 50- by 6-foot gangway approaches extend to floats from wharf, with two similar gangway approaches to floats from timber-pier approaches on north side.  Wharf and one 236-foot lightering float is used for passenger-loading only, with 136- by 12-foot launch- ing ramp at southwest side of harbor.
